== Ad Completorium | Compline
S: Ecclesiasticum Officium O.P. Triduo ante Pascha (1927), pp. 130-133
R: Chorus dicat Completorium, si competens hora fuerit: alioquin, facto aliquo temporis intervallo, hora idonea cantetur.
 = The Choir says Compline, if the hour is suitable; otherwise, after some interval of time, it is sung at a suitable hour.
R: Completorium voce mediocri dicatur, ita tamen quod sonus psalmodiæ clare distincteque resonet (quod etiam abhinc omnibus Horis in psalmodia et cantu usque ad Vesperas Sabbati fiat, exceptis Matutinis, quæ solemnius sunt dicendæ).
 = Compline is said in a moderate voice, yet so that the sound of the psalmody rings out clearly and distinctly (which is also to be done from now on at all the Hours, in psalmody and chant, until Vespers of Saturday, except Matins, which are to be said more solemnly).
R: Non dicitur *Jube, domne,* nec Benedictio *Noctem quiétam,* neque Lectio *Fratres, sóbrii estóte,* neque *Confíteor,* neque ℣. *Convérte nos,* neque ℣. *Deus, in adjutórium,* sed, dicto *Pater noster,* postquam versis vultibus ad Altare Fratres se signaverint, inchoëtur:
 = There is not said *Jube, domne,* nor the Blessing *Noctem quiétam,* nor the Lesson *Fratres, sóbrii estóte,* nor the *Confíteor,* nor the ℣. *Convérte nos,* nor the ℣. *Deus, in adjutórium;* but when the *Pater noster* has been said, and the brethren, turned towards the altar, have signed themselves, there is begun:
T: {Aña} Christus factus est. {Ps. 4} Cum invocárem.
 = {Ant.} Christ became obedient… {Ps. 4}
F: Psalmus 4 Cum invocárem | Psalm 4
G: op-ten-h-ps-4 | Tonus VIII G
F: Textus et versio | Text and translation
T: Cum invocárem exaudívit me Deus iustítiæ meæ: * in tribulatióne dilatásti mihi.
 = When I called upon him, the God of my justice heard me: * when I was in distress, thou hast enlarged me.
T: Miserére mei, * et exáudi oratiónem meam.
 = Have mercy on me: * and hear my prayer.
T: Fílii hóminum, úsquequo gravi corde? * ut quid dilígitis vanitátem, et quǽritis mendácium?
 = O ye sons of men, how long will you be dull of heart? * Why do you love vanity, and seek after lying?
T: Et scitóte quóniam mirificávit Dóminus sanctum suum: * Dóminus exáudiet me cum clamávero ad eum.
 = Know ye also that the Lord hath made his holy one wonderful: * the Lord will hear me when I shall cry unto him.
T: Irascímini, et nolíte peccáre: * quæ dícitis in córdibus vestris, in cubílibus vestris compungímini.
 = Be ye angry, and sin not: * the things you say in your hearts, be sorry for them upon your beds.
T: Sacrificáte sacrifícium iustítiæ, et speráte in Dómino. * Multi dicunt: Quis osténdit nobis bona?
 = Offer up the sacrifice of justice, and trust in the Lord: * many say, Who sheweth us good things?
T: Signátum est super nos lumen vultus tui, Dómine: * dedísti lætítiam in corde meo.
 = The light of thy countenance, O Lord, is signed upon us: * thou hast given gladness in my heart.
T: A fructu fruménti, vini, et ólei sui * multiplicáti sunt.
 = By the fruit of their corn, their wine, and oil, * they are multiplied.
T: In pace in idípsum * dórmiam, et requiéscam;
 = In peace in the selfsame * I will sleep, and I will rest:
T: Quóniam tu, Dómine, singuláriter in spe * constituísti me.
 = For thou, O Lord, singularly * hast settled me in hope.
F/
F/
F: Psalmus 90 Qui hábitat | Psalm 90
G: op-ten-h-ps-90 | Tonus VIII G
F: Textus et versio | Text and translation
T: Qui hábitat in adiutório Altíssimi, * in protectióne Dei cæli commorábitur.
 = He that dwelleth in the aid of the most High, * shall abide under the protection of the God of Jacob.
T: Dicet Dómino: Suscéptor meus es tu, et refúgium meum: * Deus meus sperábo in eum.
 = He shall say to the Lord: Thou art my protector, and my refuge: * my God, in him will I trust.
T: Quóniam ipse liberávit me de láqueo venántium, * et a verbo áspero.
 = For he hath delivered me from the snare of the hunters: * and from the sharp word.
T: Scápulis suis obumbrábit tibi: * et sub pennis eius sperábis.
 = He will overshadow thee with his shoulders: * and under his wings thou shalt trust.
T: Scuto circúmdabit te véritas eius: * non timébis a timóre noctúrno,
 = His truth shall compass thee with a shield: * thou shalt not be afraid of the terror of the night.
T: A sagítta volánte in die, a negótio perambulánte in ténebris: * ab incúrsu, et dæmónio meridiáno.
 = Of the arrow that flieth in the day, of the business that walketh about in the dark: * of invasion, or of the noonday devil.
T: Cadent a látere tuo mille, et decem míllia a dextris tuis: * ad te autem non appropinquábit.
 = A thousand shall fall at thy side, and ten thousand at thy right hand: * but it shall not come nigh thee.
T: Verúmtamen óculis tuis considerábis: * et retributiónem peccatórum vidébis.
 = But thou shalt consider with thy eyes: * and shalt see the reward of the wicked.
T: Quóniam tu es, Dómine, spes mea: * Altíssimum posuísti refúgium tuum.
 = Because thou, O Lord, art my hope: * thou hast made the most High thy refuge.
T: Non accédet ad te malum: * et flagéllum non appropinquábit tabernáculo tuo.
 = There shall no evil come to thee: * nor shall the scourge come near thy dwelling.
T: Quóniam Ángelis suis mandávit de te: * ut custódiant te in ómnibus viis tuis.
 = For he hath given his angels charge over thee; * to keep thee in all thy ways.
T: In mánibus portábunt te: * ne forte offéndas ad lápidem pedem tuum.
 = In their hands they shall bear thee up: * lest thou dash thy foot against a stone.
T: Super áspidem, et basilíscum ambulábis: * et conculcábis leónem et dracónem.
 = Thou shalt walk upon the asp and the basilisk: * and thou shalt trample under foot the lion and the dragon.
T: Quóniam in me sperávit, liberábo eum: * prótegam eum, quóniam cognóvit nomen meum.
 = Because he hoped in me I will deliver him: * I will protect him because he hath known my name.
T: Clamábit ad me, et ego exáudiam eum: * cum ipso sum in tribulatióne: erípiam eum et glorificábo eum.
 = He shall cry to me, and I will hear him: * I am with him in tribulation, I will deliver him, and I will glorify him.
T: Longitúdine diérum replébo eum: * et osténdam illi salutáre meum.
 = I will fill him with length of days; * and I will shew him my salvation.
F/
F/
F: Psalmus 133 Ecce nunc | Psalm 133
G: op-ten-h-ps-133 | Tonus VIII G
F: Textus et versio | Text and translation
T: Ecce nunc benedícite Dóminum, * omnes servi Dómini:
 = Behold now bless ye the Lord, * all ye servants of the Lord:
T: Qui statis in domo Dómini, * in átriis domus Dei nostri.
 = Who stand in the house of the Lord, * in the courts of the house of our God.
T: In nóctibus extóllite manus vestras in sancta, * et benedícite Dóminum.
 = In the nights lift up your hands to the holy places, * and bless ye the Lord.
T: Benedícat te Dóminus ex Sion, * qui fecit cælum et terram.
 = May the Lord out of Sion bless thee, * he that made heaven and earth.
F/
F/
R: Continuo sequitur Canticum Simeonis:
 = The Canticle of Simeon follows at once:
F: Canticum Simeonis (Luc. 2) Nunc dimíttis | Canticle of Simeon (Luke 2)
G: op-ten-h-ps-nunc | Tonus VIII G
F: Textus et versio | Text and translation
T: Nunc dimíttis ✠ servum tuum, Dómine, * secúndum verbum tuum in pace:
 = Now ✠ thou dost dismiss thy servant, O Lord, * according to thy word in peace;
T: Quia vidérunt óculi mei * salutáre tuum,
 = Because my eyes have seen * thy salvation,
T: Quod parásti * ante fáciem ómnium populórum,
 = Which thou hast prepared * before the face of all peoples:
T: Lumen ad revelatiónem géntium, * et glóriam plebis tuæ Israël.
 = A light to the revelation of the Gentiles, * and the glory of thy people Israel.
F/
F/
T: {Aña} Christus factus est pro nobis obédiens usque ad mortem, mortem autem crucis.
 = {Ant.} Christ became obedient for us unto death, even the death of the Cross.
G: op-ten-h-c01 | Antiphona · VIII
L: Oratio
 = Prayer
T: ^Réspice, quǽsumus, Dómine, super hanc famíliam tuam, pro qua Dóminus noster Jesus Christus non dubitávit mánibus tradi nocéntium, et crucis subíre torméntum.
 = Look down, we beseech thee, O Lord, upon this thy family, for which our Lord Jesus Christ did not hesitate to be delivered into the hands of the wicked, and to undergo the torment of the Cross.
R: Non additur *Qui tecum,* neque *Amen,* neque *Benedicámus,* neque *Fidélium,* sed solum *Pater noster,* et *Credo.* Benedictio non datur, omittitur Ant. *Salve, Regína,* nec aspergitur Aqua benedicta.
 = *Qui tecum,* *Amen,* *Benedicámus* and *Fidélium* are not added, but only the *Pater noster* and the *Credo.* The Blessing is not given, the Antiphon *Salve, Regína* is left out, and Holy Water is not sprinkled.
